  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between CID 101985700 and FaDu, based on the shared target of multiple compounds. CID 101985700 is associated with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is a key component of the polycomb repressive complex 2 (PRC2) and is involved in epigenetic regulation. This complex is targeted by several compounds, including (2S)-3-(3,4-dihydroxyphenyl)-2-[(E)-3-[4-hydroxy-3-[(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxyphenyl]prop-2-enoyl]oxypropanoic acid, (11S,17R,18R)-17-(3,4-dimethoxyphenyl)-16-oxa-1,6,10,23-tetrazatetracyclo[9.8.6.212,15.014,18]heptacosa-12,14,26-triene-19,24-dione, and 1,3,7-Octatriene. These compounds are all linked to the FaDu target, indicating a possible mechanism by which CID 101985700 may influence FaDu through the regulation of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The evidence suggests that CID 101985700 could act as a modulator of the PRC2 complex, potentially affecting the biological processes associated with FaDu. The strength of the evidence is consistent across multiple pathways, but the exact mechanism by which CID 101985700 interacts with FaDu remains to be fully elucidated.",
